# DTF tier manifest: upload-slot-exhaustion  (GHSA-9f9r-c4w8-rjv9 and artifact-keeper#4162; both 1.11.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + profiles/limits.upload-slots.yml (GLOBAL_MAX_CONCURRENCY=32,
# UPLOAD_MAX_IN_FLIGHT_PER_PRINCIPAL=8, UPLOAD_PROGRESS_WINDOW_SECS=5,
# AK_PROXY_METADATA_BUDGET_BYTES=256 MiB) + profiles/upstreams.mock-composer-v1.yml
# (a stdlib-python Composer v1 provider upstream on 172.16.<slot>.72).
#
# THE FIXES (1.11.0, artifact-keeper#4588 and #4170; red on 1.10.0)
#   GHSA-9f9r: upload routes are exempt from the wall-clock request timeout,
#     and nothing else bounded how long a client could take to send a body. A
#     writer could open uploads, send headers and a byte, and hold every
#     GLOBAL_MAX_CONCURRENCY slot; every other request, /health and /ready
#     included, was then shed 503. The fix adds a progress floor (408), a
#     per-principal in-flight cap (429 + Retry-After) and a probe bypass of
#     the global pool, and streams Git LFS uploads to scratch disk.
#   #4162: the Composer v1 provider fallback held a 128 MiB reservation of
#     the shared buffered-metadata budget while it reserved again for each
#     provider-includes file and the package document. N concurrent callers
#     with a budget of N reservations deadlocked until the 120 s request
#     timeout, stalling every format's buffered metadata. The profile lowers
#     the budget to two reservations so eight callers deadlock for sure.
#
# Every socket the oracle holds is driven by fixtures/slot_hold.py (stdlib
# python, bounded waits), so a red backend fails a case instead of hanging.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem limits.upload-slots upstreams.mock-composer-v1"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="true"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
